        "original_id": "7b0b7b18-a623-539f-8cde-33e26ef1b533",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Der Freischütz, Il trovatore, Magic Hunter\n- People: Carl Maria von Weber, Friedrich Kind, Giuseppe Verdi, Salvadore Cammarano, Antonio García Gutiérrez, Ildikó Enyedi, Giovanni Guicciardi\n- Roles: Count di Luna\n\nFacts:\n- Der Freischütz, Op. 77, J. 277, is a German opera with spoken dialogue in three acts by Carl Maria von Weber with a libretto by Friedrich Kind.\n- In 1836, Antonio García Gutiérrez wrote the play El trovador, which later served as the basis for Il trovatore.\n- Il trovatore is an opera in four acts by Giuseppe Verdi with an Italian libretto largely written by Salvadore Cammarano.\n- Giovanni Guicciardi is best remembered for creating the role of Count di Luna in Verdi's Il trovatore.\n- Magic Hunter is a 1994 Hungarian-Swiss-French fantasy film written and directed by Ildikó Enyedi.\n- Magic Hunter was loosely inspired by the opera Der Freischütz.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
